# REVIEW EXAMPLE ONLY. No job is installed or enabled by this file.
# Copy ONLY the application-host block to its separately reviewed scheduler;
# copy ONLY the watchdog block to an independent off-platform host/scheduler.
# Do not paste both into the application host or add a second sender job.
MAILTO=""
SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# APPLICATION HOST — one minute, one bounded existing sender/reminder endpoint.
# Actual Node path, app path, credential path, lock filesystem and host limits
# must be verified first. Secrets stay in protected environment files, not URLs.
# * * * * * /reviewed/node --env-file=/reviewed/private/email-sender.env /reviewed/app/scripts/run-email-automation.mjs --config /reviewed/private/email-sender.json --execute >> /reviewed/logs/email-sender.jsonl 2>&1

# INDEPENDENT WATCHDOG HOST — separate host, scheduler and contact transport.
# This host needs only email-automation-watchdog.mjs and Node's standard library.
# * * * * * /reviewed/node --env-file=/reviewed/private/email-watchdog.env /reviewed/monitor/email-automation-watchdog.mjs --config /reviewed/private/email-watchdog.json --execute >> /reviewed/logs/email-watchdog.jsonl 2>&1

# INDEPENDENT SYSTEM MONITOR — separate state/lock and reviewed system mapping.
# See system-health-setup-proposal.md. This does not add another email sender.
# * * * * * /reviewed/node --env-file=/reviewed/private/system-watchdog.env /reviewed/monitor/email-automation-watchdog.mjs --config /reviewed/private/system-watchdog.json --execute >> /reviewed/logs/system-watchdog.jsonl 2>&1

# Each CLI re-executes itself under Linux util-linux:
# flock --no-fork --nonblock --conflict-exit-code 75 <configured-lock-path> node ...
# OS process death releases ownership. There is no sticky owner-file lock and
# no age-based stealing. Busy exits 75 without HTTP work. Linux flock support,
# shared lock paths and process/signal behavior remain enablement evidence.
# JSON mappings must explicitly enable reviewed scopes; sample docs are disabled.
# Do not install these lines or contact real services during local verification.
